ounting of the tension  between the two most influential  countries of the 21st century you ask  whether we're headed to a new Cold War  some wonder whether we're already in it  I mean I think when we were writing the  book we just and finished it which is  only in the beginning of this year  things were headed toward a new Cold War  then you had Co vid on top of that and  then you had Hong Kong on top of that  and so yes it's very possible we are in  the in the midst or the beginning of a  Cold War and something that I think will  last beyond whoever wins the presidency  how long gosh I mean you know the last  Cold War lasted for 40 or 50 years I  mean we're talking about long term  changes the book takes readers back to  China's rise in the 1980s and 90s  following the devastation of the Mao  Zedong  era when China suffered terribly for  more than 30 years during in after World  War two China's returned a superpower  status in the early part of this century  was completed in cooperation with the US  until a couple things happened first the  global financial crisis of 2008 and 2009  badly soured the relationship then in  2012 she shin pang came to power there  have been so many famous or infamous  Chinese leaders over the decades  how does Xi Jinping figure into all that  Xi Jinping is the most powerful Chinese  leader at least since Deng Xiaoping and  maybe arguably since now  cheese consolidation of power and  determination to build the biggest  economy in the world  put China on an even more direct  collision course with America  then came the US election of 2016 this  is a battle that has gone on before the  Trump administration and will go on for  decades after but how has this current  administration impacted what's happened  now it intensified everything president  Trump's decision to start a trade war  using tariffs was the most extreme  economic provocation since the 1930s it  is the largest deficit of any country in  the history of our world and perhaps  